SWEET dev overlay whiteout + BT hot-reload paths (patch 0280, on top of 0117/0154; user 2026-11-09: one standard root, hot reload).
An EMPTY entry with mode 0xFFFF REMOVES its path: a file an earlier overlay or devsh push ADDED (tools/overlay_std.py emits it only
for paths the flashed standard root image does not contain). Kernel-side limits: only below /usr/local/ or /private/var/dev/ or
exactly /usr/lib/libsweetgl.dylib (never the rest of /usr/lib), only a regular file, never one with a .sweetorig (that file came
from the root image), every parent a real directory (NOFOLLOW, none created); the kernel cannot tell a never-replaced root-image file, so keeping whiteouts off those is the host tools' job (review 0280 F1). Logs `SWEET DEV: removed|absent|refused <path>`.
Kernels without 0280 refuse such an entry as "mode above 0777" (harmless). Also allows exactly /Applications/BTApp.app/BTApp and
/private/var/mobile/Library/Preferences/com.apple.MobileBluetooth.debug.plist (tools/devd.c k_allow[] stays equal, H3).
File writes on userdata only (rule 1 partition), no hardware register.

